SUMMARY:Upper Calisthenics + Hypertrophy
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3350 kcal\, 165 g protein\, 455 g carbs\, 9
 5 g fat\nCategory: gym\nRun volume: 0 km\nAdjustments:\n- Adjusted for mo
 derate recovery constraint.\n- Light active commute counted.\n- Adjusted 
 for temporary low-back recovery constraint.\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 5 min easy car
 dio\, shoulder circles\, light rows\, and scap pull-ups.\n\nMain Work:\n-
  Progression: double progression\; beat total quality reps before adding 
 load or a set\, keeping most work at RPE 8-9. Moderate recovery constrain
 t: reduce volume by 25-40%\, cap hard sets at RPE 7\, and leave the gym/r
 un fresher than planned. Light active commute: 30 min calm cycling each w
 ay counts as easy aerobic load\; keep hard sets at the prescribed RPE. Te
 mporary low-back recovery constraint: cap loaded work at RPE 6-7 and stop
  if symptoms rise.\n- Pull-ups: 5 x 4-8 or 20-30 total quality reps at RP
 E 8.\n- Dips or push-ups: 3 x 8-15 at RPE 8-9\, stop before shoulder posi
 tion changes.\n- One-arm dumbbell row or inverted row: 3 x 8-12 at RPE 8 
 paired with incline dumbbell press 2-3 x 8-12 at RPE 8.\n- Core finisher:
  lateral raises plus hanging leg raises 2-3 sets each at RPE 8. Temporary
  low-back recovery constraint: avoid loaded hinging and heavy bracing\; u
 se machines or supported positions where possible.\n\nFueling:\n- Hit dai
 ly macros\, keep protein near target\, and place carbohydrates before and
  after training.\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; add mob
 ility if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
