 ain Work:\n- Progression: add power volume only when jumps stay crisp and
  knees stay quiet the next day\; sprint RPE 7-8. Reduce volume by 25-40% 
 before adding intensity. Low-back ramp: start lightly and add load only w
 hen the next morning is symptom-free.\n- Plyometrics: pogos 3 x 20 sec\, 
 low broad jumps 4 x 2\, and med-ball slams 4 x 5 at crisp RPE 6-7 if avai
 lable.\n- Hill sprint technique: 4-6 x 8-10 sec at sprint RPE 7-8.\n- Fun
 ctional work: sled push if easy to set up or farmer carries 4 x 30 m at R
 PE 7. Keep carries light and skip them if the low back feels loaded.\n- C
 ore: crawling 3 x 20 m or dead bug 3 x 8 per side. Low-back ramp: no dead
 lifts or hyperextensions\; start lightly and keep supported posterior-cha
 in work pain-free.\n\nRun:\n- Planned running volume: 3 km.\n\nFueling:\n
 - Hit daily macros\, keep protein near target\, and place carbohydrates b
 efore and after training.\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\
 ; add mobility if joints feel stiff.
